-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for Z2 (doc/cross-term.pdf,
-- Definition 1, Lemma 2): one entry per declaration, checked entry by entry
-- against the text.  Every opening is a by-definition step of the text:
-- computing xor, not, the parity rhoN / rhoZ and the operations of Integers
-- (sucNeg, sucZ, predPos, predZ, addP, addN, add) on constructors; code by
-- cases; isProp, isSet; the carriers of Z2ab and intAb and Hom (the type of
-- rho, twoH, zeroH, two-zero).
Z2.ZZ:
Z2.xor:
Z2.not-not: Base.not
Z2.xor-assoc: Z2.xor Base.not
Z2.xor-comm: Z2.xor Base.not
Z2.xor-unitr: Z2.xor Base.not
Z2.xor-invr: Z2.xor Base.not
Z2.xor-not: Z2.xor
Z2.code:
Z2.code-prop: Z2.code Prelude.isProp
Z2.code-refl: Z2.code
Z2.code-eq: Z2.code
Z2.bool-set: Prelude.isSet
Z2.Z2ab:
Z2.rhoN:
Z2.rhoZ:
Z2.rho-sucNeg: Base.not Z2.rhoN Integers.sucNeg Z2.rhoZ
Z2.rho-suc: Z2.rhoZ Base.not Integers.sucZ Z2.rhoN
Z2.rho-predPos: Z2.rhoN Base.not Integers.predPos Z2.rhoZ
Z2.rho-pred: Base.not Z2.rhoZ Integers.predZ Z2.rhoN
Z2.rho-addP: Integers.addP Z2.rhoN Base.not Integers.sucZ
Z2.rho-addN: Integers.addN Z2.rhoN Base.not Integers.predZ
Z2.rho-hom: Integers.add Z2.rhoZ
Z2.rho: Integers.intAb Z2.Z2ab EMMaps.Hom
Z2.twoH: EMMaps.Hom
Z2.zeroH: EMMaps.Hom
Z2.two-zero: Z2.Z2ab Z2.twoH Z2.zeroH
